<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">California</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">California is a state on the Pacific coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the country's most populous. Colonised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> from 1769 with missions and presidios as Alta California, it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1821 and was ceded to the United States after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-american-war">Mexican–American War</a> in 1848. The gold rush that began that year drew hundreds of thousands of migrants, and California became a state in 1850.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/california.jpg" alt="California" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Donald Graeme Kelley Vectorization: Devin Cook · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_California.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
